column7:
Open Data Bootcamp DataTeka has been developed for the beginners and features open data examples from the National Open Data Portal, with a goal to increase data literacy. Reuse case URL: http://rbootcamp.rbind.io/general/ It uses various open data sets from the National Open Data Portal. Reuse case description: This bootcamp offers opportunity for participants to: learn to explore, visualize, and analyse data in a reproducible and sharable manner;
Develop an understanding and basic knowledge to model data, to identify patterns and make predictions;
Gain experience in data wrangling, exploratory data analysis and data visualization, and effective communication of results;
Work on the case studies inspired by real problems and based on open data. The second example is Petlja Foundation, which uses open data sets for their course for data officers. Reuse URL: https://petlja.org/sr-Latn-RS/biblioteka/r/kursevi/DataOfficer-jupyter Reuse case description: This manual is intended for civil servants who, as part of their work, create data-driven analyses or use, or could proactively use, the potential of large amounts of official and open data from various sources for decision-making purposes. It is also intended for officials involved in shaping public policies and regulations. Up to date, around 500 public servants finished courses for Data officers, data visualizationa and general course on open data.
